==Cebuano==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ceb|ug}}
* {{alt|ceb|'g||contraction, appended to the preceding word}}

===Etymology===
Standardized form of {{m|ceb|ug}} as an article in contrast to its conjunctional function.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ceb-IPA|ug}}

===Article===
{{head|ceb|article}}

# {{n-g|indefinite indirect marker for nouns other than personal names.}}
#: {{cot|ceb|sa|lb=for definite nouns}}
#: {{ux|ceb|'''Mi'''kaon '''og isda''' ang iring.|The cat ate '''''a'' fish'''.}}
#: {{ux|ceb|'''Gi'''kaon '''og iring''' ang isda.|'''''A'' cat''' ate the fish.}}
# {{n-g|refers to motion towards an indefinite location}}:
#: {{ux|ceb|Moadto siya '''og''' merkado unya.|He's going '''to ''a''''' market later.|inline=1}}
# {{n-g|refers to accompaniment with an indefinite partner or object}}: [[with]] [[a]]
#: {{syn|ceb|[[uban#Cebuano|uban]] ('''og'''/[[ang#Cebuano|ang]])|[[kuyog#Cebuano|kuyog]] (og/[[ang#Cebuano|ang]])}}
#: {{ux|ceb|Nagpakuyog si Juan '''og''' guwardiya.|Juan went '''with ''a''''' security guard.|inline=1}}
# {{n-g|refers to an indefinite tool or instrument used for doing}}: [[with]], [[through]], [[by]]
#: {{syn|ceb|[[gamit#Cebuano|gamit]] ([[ang#Cebuano|ang]])}}
#: {{ux|ceb|Iyang gibunalan '''og''' silhig.|He striked him '''with ''a''''' broom.|inline=1}}
# {{n-g|shows relation between two grammatical parts}}:
## {{n-g|preceding infinitives}} {{q|replacing a prefix {{m|ceb|pag-}}}}
##: {{ux|ceb|Naglisod ko '''og''' saka.|I had a hard time going up.|inline=1}}
## {{n-g|with adjectives of manner}}
##: {{ux|ceb|Nilakaw siya '''og''' kusog.|He walked away fast.|inline=1}}
## {{n-g|after {{m|ceb|ayaw|t=don't}}}}
##: {{ux|ceb|Ayaw '''og''' adto.|Don't go.|inline=1}}
# {{q|adjective + '''og''' + noun}} {{n-g|having, possessing as an attribute}}:
#: {{syn|ceb|may}}
#: {{ux|ceb|Dako og bukton.|Having big arms.|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|ceb|Kanindot niya og mata!|What beautiful eyes s/he has!|inline=1}}

====Usage notes====
* See usage notes under {{m|ceb|sa}}.

